BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[FREE] A Slice of Literary Orange -  Walter Mosley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T193000
DTSTAMP:20261028T145611Z
UID:59e8c84a95e2b08660af8264a76c7727@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,family,Author Visits
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: OCPL - Tustin Branch\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mont
 hs\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nA Slice of Literary Orange presents: Walter 
 Mosley. Walter Mosley is one of America’s most celebrated writers. He wa
 s given the 2020 National Book Award’s Medal for Distinguished Contribut
 ion to American Letters\, named a Grand Master of the Mystery Writers of A
 merica\, and honored with the Anisfield-Wolf Award\, a Grammy\, a PEN USA 
 Lifetime Achievement Award\, the Robert Kirsch Award\, numerous Edgars\, a
 nd several NAACP Image Awards. His work has been translated into twenty-fi
 ve languages. He has published fiction and nonfiction in The New Yorker\, 
 Playboy\, and The Nation. As an executive producer\, he adapted his novel 
 The Last Days of Ptolemy Grey for AppleTV . He co-wrote the adaptation of 
 his novel The Man in My Basement to stream on Hulu\, and he served as a wr
 iter and executive producer for FX’s Snowfall. He divides his time betwe
 en Brooklyn and Santa Monica.\n\nTustin Library 345 E. Main St\, Tustin\, 
 CA 92780\n\nLimited complimentary books available\, while supplies last.\n
 \nAdmission does not guarantee a free copy. No registration required. Earl
 y arrival suggested.\\n\\nMore info: https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/1768621
 6
LOCATION:Tustin
URL:https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/17686216
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: A Slice of Literary Orange -  Walter Mosley
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:In 2 hours: A Slice of Literary Orange -  Walter Mosley
TRIGGER:-PT2H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
