BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Recycling Day at Pretend City
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T130000
DTSTAMP:20261028T145611Z
UID:a5d669864f2a4ee1f36636e133012f24@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:children,play,toddler,museum,family
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nPretend City Children&#8217\;s Muse
 um teamed up with OC Waste &amp\; Recycling to bring hands-on vermicompost
 ing education to young learners! Through interactive presentations and act
 ivities\, kids explore how worms help recycle food scraps into nutrient-ri
 ch compost\, leaning firsthand how small actions can make a big impact for
  our planet! Together\, we&#8217\;re making organics recycling fun\, engag
 ing\, and accessible for the next generation of environmental stewards.\nT
 ime: 11am-1pm\nIncluded with Museum admission Activities take place throug
 hout the day while supplies last.\n*Events and times are subject to change
 .\n\nAbout the play partner: \nOC Wast &amp\; Recycle serves the County&#
 8217\;s solid waste disposal needs by providing waste management services
 \, operating public landfills\, protecting the local environment\, investi
 ng in renewable energy enterprises and promoting recycling in order to ens
 ure a safe and healthy community for current and future generations. OCWR 
 also provides education\, outreach\, and sustainability programs that help
  residents reduce waste and support state and local mandates.\nFrequently 
 Asked Questions\nWhat is Getting Wiggly with Composting program?\nGetting 
 Wiggly with Composting is a hands-on environmental learning experience at 
 Pretend City Children’s Museum in Irvine\, California\, where children d
 iscover how worms turn food scraps into nutrient-rich compost through verm
 icomposting.\nIs this activity included with admission?\nYes. The vermicom
 posting activities are included with regular museum admission.\nWhat ages 
 is this program best for?\nThe experience is designed for children ages 3
 –12 and their families.\nWill kids see real worms?\nYes. Children can le
 arn about real worms and how they help break down food scraps into compost
 .\\n\\nMore info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events/recycling-day-at-pret
 end-city/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/recycling-day-at-pretend-city/
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Recycling Day at Pretend City
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:In 2 hours: Recycling Day at Pretend City
TRIGGER:-PT2H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
