DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nDive into a fun\, hands-on food adv
 enture inspired by Hawai‘i’s ocean life with Native Hawaiian Chef Char
 les Akau of Mila’s Kitchen Hawaii! Keiki will create an adorable edible 
 Hawaiian sea turtle and dolphin using fresh fruits\, snacks\, and other ki
 d-friendly ingredients. Hosted by Chef Charles Akau of Mila’s Kitchen Ha
 wai‘i\, this interactive class introduces little ones to creativity\, fo
 od presentation\, and the beautiful animals found under the Hawaiian sea. 
 Each child will leave with their own ocean-inspired charcuterie creation t
 o enjoy. Perfect for curious little chefs who love animals\, snacks\, and
  hands-on fun!\nTime: 11am and 2:30PM\nSpace is limited! Book your tickets
  now\; this program is included in museum admission.\n*Events and dates ar
 e subject to change.\nAbout the play partner:\nMila’s Kitchen Hawaii Jou
 rney to the islands at Mila&#8217\;s Kitchen Hawaii\, where Hawaiian cultu
 re blends seamlessly with Southern California influences. Helmed by Native
  Hawaiian Chef Charles Akau IV\, this vibrant culinary experience is inspi
 red by the “Legacy of Aloha.” The menu’s authentic island flavors wi
 ll transport visitors to paradise with every bite.\\n\\nMore info: https:/
 /www.pretendcity.org/events/cooking-in-the-city-6/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/cooking-in-the-city-6/
